</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Dibben</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Muirhead</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Modelling supply and demand influences on the use of health care: implications for deriving a needs-based capitation formula</article-title><source>Health Economics</source><year>2003</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>985</fpage><lpage>1004</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14673809</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/hec.830</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gerdtham</surname><given-names>U-G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Equity in health care utilization: Further tests based on hurdle models and Swedish micro data</article-title><source>Health Economics</source><year>1997</year><volume>6</volume><fpage>303</fpage><lpage>319</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9226147</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/(SICI)1099-1050(199705)6:3&#x0003c;303::AID-HEC270&#x0003e;3.0.CO;2-P</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pohlmeier</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Ulrich</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>An econometric model of the two-part decisionmaking process in the demand for health care</article-title><source>Journal of Human Resources</source><year>1995</year><volume>30</volume><fpage>339</fpage><lpage>361</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2307/146123</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cameron</surname><given-names>AC</given-names></name><name><surname>Trivedi</surname><given-names>PK</given-names></name></person-group><source>Regression analysis of count data</source><year>1998</year><publisher-name